; MAC-HYG-8's first hole, made loud (AX3032, 2026-08-15).
;
; A template's free identifier means what it meant WHERE THE MACRO WAS
; WRITTEN. For a macro defined in a module that is enforced by
; qualification - the reference becomes `Mod$name`, which nothing at a
; call site can shadow - and `tests/selfhost/364-macro-definition-site.ax`
; pins it. A macro defined in the ENTRY FILE has nothing to qualify
; to, because the entry file's declarations are deliberately left
; bare, so a binding of the same name at the invocation captured the
; reference.
;
; Measured before this code existed: this file's `main` answered 0 -
; the local's value - where the macro's own `helper` answers 40, at
; exit 0, with no diagnostic from any pass. That is the worst shape a
; defect takes here, and the permanent fix is scope sets (MAC-HYG-9),
; which change what an identifier IS. Until then the capture refuses.
;
; Three diagnostics, and their SHAPE is the point: the check fires per
; INVOCATION, not per macro. `shadowedTwice` reports twice from one
; `let`, and `safe` - the same macro where nothing shadows it - is not
; reported at all and still answers the macro's own `helper`.
(macro (useHelper v) (helper v))

(:: helper (-> Int Int))

(fn (helper x) (* x 10))

(:: shadowed Int)

(fn (shadowed)
  (let ((helper 
    (lambda (y) 0)
  ))
    (useHelper 4)
  )
)

(:: shadowedTwice Int)

(fn (shadowedTwice)
  (let ((helper 
    (lambda (y) 1)
  ))
    (+ (useHelper 1) (useHelper 2))
  )
)

(:: safe Int)

(fn (safe) (useHelper 4))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ shadowed safe))
